# Tracer: compiler unary function set and proof-carrying application
#
# Before (required an incidental wrapper):
# sketch:
#     forall s, S set, x s, f fn(y s) S:
#         f(x) = f(x)
# Former behavior: the function tracer was nested in `sketch`, and compiler
# flattened sketch statements instead of preserving their source scope.
#
# Now: the forall is a direct top-level fact. s and S become Litex.Set values.
# x and f retain independent Lean
# carriers plus their verifier-created Litex.In hypotheses. Each generated
# Litex.fnApply consumes both the exact function-membership FactId proof and
# the exact argument-membership WD proof selected for that source occurrence.
#
# Boundary: this first slice supports one named unary application layer with no
# extra domain facts. Anonymous functions, multiple parameters, domain clauses,
# and curried return function sets remain fail-closed. The focused Rust
# negative test changes `x s` to `x S`; Litex rejects `f(x)` before emission
# because no proof of `x $in s` exists.
#
# Evidence:
# target/release/litex -compact -strict -runner -f lean/examples/4_FunctionSet.lit
# cd lean && ./compiler.sh compile examples/4_FunctionSet.lit
# cd lean && ./compiler.sh check examples && lake env lean examples/4_FunctionSet.lean

forall s, S set, x s, f fn(y s) S:
    f(x) = f(x)
